---
import { site } from '../../data/site';
import { routes } from '../../i18n';
import Legal from '../../layouts/Legal.astro';

const { company } = site;
const summary = [
  `Your personal data is controlled by ${company.name}`,
  'The website does not set cookies and does not use analytics or advertising tools.',
  'The enquiry form does not send data to our server. It prepares a message that you send from your own email app.',
  'Before sharing full property details we verify your identity, as required by anti-money laundering law.',
  'You have the right to access, rectify and erase your data, to restrict processing, to object and to lodge a complaint with the Polish supervisory authority (UODO).',
];
---

<Legal lang="en" route="privacy" title="Privacy policy" summary={summary}>
  <section>
    <h2>Data controller</h2>
    <p>
      The controller of your personal data is <strong>{company.name}</strong>, registered office at {company.address},
      entered in the register of entrepreneurs of the Polish National Court Register under KRS number {company.krs},
      tax identification number (NIP) {company.nip}, statistical number (REGON) {company.regon}, share capital
      {' '}{company.capital.en} (the “Controller”).
    </p>
    <p>
      For any matter concerning personal data, write to{' '}
      <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>{' '}or by post to the registered office.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>What data we process</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Enquiry data:</strong> full name, phone number or email address, the content of your message and the email
        address you send it from. The form on this website does not transmit data to our server. It prepares a ready message
        that you send yourself from your email app.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Identity verification data:</strong> details from your identity document and other information required by
        the Polish Act of 1 March 2018 on counteracting money laundering and terrorist financing, collected before full
        property details are shared or a brokerage agreement is signed.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Technical data:</strong> IP address, date and time of the visit and browser type, recorded automatically in
        server logs by the hosting provider.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Purposes and legal bases</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        Replying to your enquiry and contact before an agreement is concluded: Article 6(1)(b) GDPR (steps taken at your
        request prior to entering into a contract) and Article 6(1)(f) GDPR (the Controller’s legitimate interest in
        conducting correspondence).
      </li>
      <li>
        Identity verification and customer due diligence: Article 6(1)(c) GDPR in connection with the Act on counteracting
        money laundering and terrorist financing. A real estate broker is an obligated institution under that Act.
      </li>
      <li>Performance of a real estate brokerage agreement: Article 6(1)(b) GDPR.</li>
      <li>Establishing, exercising or defending legal claims: Article 6(1)(f) GDPR.</li>
      <li>Security and proper operation of the website (server logs): Article 6(1)(f) GDPR.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Retention periods</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Enquiry correspondence: until the enquiry is handled, then until any related claims become time-barred.</li>
      <li>
        Identity verification records: 5 years from the first day of the year following the year in which the business
        relationship ended or the occasional transaction was carried out (Article 49 of the Act on counteracting money
        laundering and terrorist financing).
      </li>
      <li>Brokerage agreement data: for the term of the agreement and until related claims become time-barred.</li>
      <li>Server logs: {company.logRetention}.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Recipients of data</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Website hosting provider: {company.hosting}.</li>
      <li>Email provider: {company.mailbox}.</li>
      <li>Law firms and notaries, to the extent necessary to complete a transaction.</li>
      <li>
        Public authorities where the law requires disclosure, including the General Inspector of Financial Information.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      We do not transfer data outside the European Economic Area. If a service provider processes data outside the EEA, this
      is based on a European Commission adequacy decision or standard contractual clauses.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Your rights</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>access to your data and a copy of it (Article 15 GDPR),</li>
      <li>rectification (Article 16 GDPR),</li>
      <li>erasure (Article 17 GDPR),</li>
      <li>restriction of processing (Article 18 GDPR),</li>
      <li>portability of data processed under a contract (Article 20 GDPR),</li>
      <li>objection to processing based on legitimate interest (Article 21 GDPR),</li>
      <li>
        a complaint to the President of the Personal Data Protection Office (UODO), ul. Stawki 2, 00-193 Warszawa, Poland.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      The right to erasure does not cover records that we must keep under the Act on counteracting money laundering and
      terrorist financing.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Providing data</h2>
    <p>
      Providing data in an enquiry is voluntary, but we cannot reply without it. Providing identity verification data is a
      condition for sharing full property details and concluding an agreement, because the law requires it.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Cookies and third-party tools</h2>
    <p>
      The website does not set cookies, does not use analytics or advertising tools and does not load resources from
      third-party servers. Fonts are hosted together with the website. If this changes, we will update this policy and ask
      for consent where the law requires it.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Automated decisions</h2>
    <p>We do not make decisions based solely on automated processing, including profiling.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
    <p>
      The current version of this policy is always available on this page. The rules for using the website are set out in
      the{' '}
      <a href={routes.terms.en}>terms</a>.
    </p>
  </section>
</Legal>
